<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>A Formal Proof on the Primacy of Mask Attention</h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.1 </span>Preliminaries and Notation</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure the rigor of the proof, we first define the symbols and notation used throughout this section.</p>
<ul id="A1.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input Sequence:</span> The input sequence <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of embeddings for <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, where <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the embedding dimension. The sequence <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is partitioned into two parts:</p>
<ul id="A1.I5.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt:</span> <math id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{p}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{p}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{p}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{p}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, with its set of token indices denoted as <math id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mask:</span> <math id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{m}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{m}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, with its set of token indices denoted as <math id="A1.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The full sequence is a concatenation <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=[X_{p},X_{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=[X_{p},X_{m}]</annotation></semantics></math>, with a total length of <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n_{p}+n_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n_{p}+n_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transformer Layer:</span> A standard Transformer model consists of <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> identical layers stacked on top of each other. Let <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the output hidden state of the <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer, where <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the initial embedding as the output of the 0-th layer, i.e., <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}=X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}=X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intra-Layer Computation:</span> The computation within layer <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented as a function, <span id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Block</span>, which takes the output of the previous layer <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> as input:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l)}=\text{Block}(h^{(l-1)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Block</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l)}=\text{Block}(h^{(l-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To analyze the information flow, we can abstract the update process of each layer. The output of layer <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of its input and an update term <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l)}=h^{(l-1)}+\Delta^{(l)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l)}=h^{(l-1)}+\Delta^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the total update contributed by the sub-layers (MHA and FFN) of layer <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Comparison of token selection strategies on <span id="A1.T7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">gsm8k</span> with <span id="A1.T7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">budget=128</span>.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T7.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T7.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T7.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Token Selection Strategy</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T7.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Score (%)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">SnapKV</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">64.90</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Prompt-Voting</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">60.35</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Mask-Voting</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T7.6.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">68.08</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">All-Voting</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">66.64</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.2 </span>Proposition</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any mask token <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, its final hidden state <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(L)}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(L)}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, which directly determines the predictive logits, can be precisely expressed as the sum of its initial embedding <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and the cumulative updates from all <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers of the model. Within these updates, the Multi-Head Attention (MHA) mechanism serves as the sole channel for the mask token to incorporate information from the prompt tokens. Consequently, the attention scores originating from mask queries are the most direct and fundamental indicators of the importance of prompt information for the model’s generative process.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Effect of mask token position on voting performance (<span id="A1.T8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">budget=256</span>). The best score in each column and the best overall average are highlighted in <span id="A1.T8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</figcaption>
