</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.3 </span>Proof</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof proceeds in three steps. First, we establish the central role of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{m}^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{m}^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> by considering the model’s objective function. Second, we derive the compositional structure of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{m}^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{m}^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> through a recursive expansion. Finally, we analyze the components of this structure to demonstrate the unique role of the attention mechanism.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: The Inference Objective and Decisive Computations</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During inference, the objective of the model is to predict a sequence of tokens for the positions specified by the mask index set, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. This generative process begins with the computation of the final hidden states, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, for the entire sequence. The language model head (LM Head), a linear projection matrix <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{out}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times|V|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{out}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times|V|}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V|</annotation></semantics></math> is the vocabulary size), then maps these hidden states to logit vectors:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Logits}=h^{(L)}\cdot W_{out}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Logits</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Logits}=h^{(L)}\cdot W_{out}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A “softmax” function is subsequently applied to the logits at each position to yield a probability distribution over the vocabulary.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Critically, for the task at hand, our interest lies exclusively in the logits at the active mask positions (<math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>), since all other tokens—whether part of the original prompt (<math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>) or already unmasked in prior steps—are considered fixed context. Therefore, the generative process, whether it be greedy decoding or sampling, is performed exclusively on the probability distributions corresponding to the mask positions. This implies that the quantities of interest, which solely determine the generated output, are the final hidden states of the mask tokens, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{h_{m}^{(L)}\mid m\in S_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{h_{m}^{(L)}\mid m\in S_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Recursive Expansion of the Hidden State</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the abstract update rule <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l)}=h^{(l-1)}+\Delta^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l)}=h^{(l-1)}+\Delta^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can perform a recursive expansion (a telescoping sum) for the final hidden state <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{m}^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{m}^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> of any mask token <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{m}^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{m}^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h_{m}^{(L-1)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h_{m}^{(L-1)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(h_{m}^{(L-2)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L-1)})+\Delta_{m}^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(h_{m}^{(L-2)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L-1)})+\Delta_{m}^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h_{m}^{(L-2)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L-1)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h_{m}^{(L-2)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L-1)}+\Delta_{m}^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center" colspan="2"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h_{m}^{(0)}+\sum_{l=1}^{L}\Delta_{m}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h_{m}^{(0)}+\sum_{l=1}^{L}\Delta_{m}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This expansion is the mathematical centerpiece of our proof, showing that the final representation is an accumulation of updates upon its initial state.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Analysis of the Update Components</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now analyze the composition of the cumulative update term <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l=1}^{L}\Delta_{m}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l=1}^{L}\Delta_{m}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each layer’s update <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{m}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{m}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of contributions from the MHA and FFN sub-layers: <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{m}^{(l)}=\text{MHA}_{m}^{(l)}+\text{FFN}_{m}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>MHA</mtext><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mtext>FFN</mtext><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{m}^{(l)}=\text{MHA}_{m}^{(l)}+\text{FFN}_{m}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contribution of the Feed-Forward Network (FFN):</span> The FFN is a position-wise transformation. Its computation for token <math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of all other tokens <math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the FFN can only process and non-linearly transform the information already present in <math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>; it cannot introduce new information from the prompt.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contribution of Multi-Head Attention (MHA):</span> The MHA mechanism is fundamentally different. The output for token <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AttnOut}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>AttnOut</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AttnOut}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a weighted sum of the Value vectors <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> of all tokens in the sequence:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AttnOut}_{m}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\alpha_{mj}V_{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>AttnOut</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AttnOut}_{m}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\alpha_{mj}V_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I6.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the attention weight <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{mj}=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{Q_{m}K_{j}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{mj}=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{Q_{m}K_{j}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. The summation index <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> spans all tokens, including those in the prompt (<math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in S_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in S_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>). This demonstrates that MHA is the <span id="A1.I6.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exclusive</span> mechanism that allows for information exchange between different token positions. For a mask token <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, only through MHA can it interact with prompt tokens <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in S_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in S_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> to aggregate relevant information.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Combining these points, we see that within the final representation <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{m}^{(L)}=h_{m}^{(0)}+\sum_{l=1}^{L}(\text{MHA}_{m}^{(l)}+\text{FFN}_{m}^{(l)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>MHA</mtext><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mtext>FFN</mtext><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{m}^{(L)}=h_{m}^{(0)}+\sum_{l=1}^{L}(\text{MHA}_{m}^{(l)}+\text{FFN}_{m}^{(l)})</annotation></semantics></math>, the MHA term is the sole channel through which information from the prompt can be incorporated into the mask token’s representation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.4 </span>Conclusion and Implication</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In conclusion, our theoretical proof establishes the primacy of attention guided by mask queries within the generative paradigm of dLLMs. By demonstrating that this mechanism is the indispensable information bridge from context to target, our findings provide a robust theoretical foundation for novel inference strategies, such as the KV cache selection method proposed in this work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
